{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "97", "x": 0.904017983697097, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.029725264906538765, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "to sense their environment: they can't yet recognise and move the pieces on a real", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.8265305719672376, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "chessboard as cleverly as a child can. Later this century, however, their more", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.8260121032758466, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "advanced successors may relate to their surroundings, and to people, as adeptly", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.825968325120572, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "as we do. Moral questions then arise. … Should we feel guilty about exploiting", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.8264922276345146, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "[sophisticated robots]? Should we fret if they are underemployed, frustrated, or", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.8260337360410994, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "bored?'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.26469857438786853, "w": 0.08147765730070457, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Wolpert's response to the question about machine intelligence outstripping", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3030039694975767, "w": 0.8261859855974996, "h": 0.018822616509687834, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "human intelligence was this: 'In a limited sense it already has. Machines can", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.33133430071101805, "w": 0.8267665844108962, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "already navigate, remember and search for items with an ability that far outstrips", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3596646507851557, "w": 0.8260337360410994, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "humans. However, there is no machine that can identify visual objects or speech", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.38799500085929334, "w": 0.8259465898303653, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "with the reliability and flexibility of humans. … Expecting a machine close to the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.41632538865482344, "w": 0.8266304312722434, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "creative intelligence of a human within the next 50 years would be highly", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4446557764503536, "w": 0.8260880742666159, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "ambitious.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.47301087175797835, "w": 0.11493864958026796, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Richardson believes that our fear of machines becoming too advanced has more", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5493990303187956, "w": 0.8260772066215126, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "to do with human nature than anything intrinsic to the machines themselves. In", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5777294181143257, "w": 0.826011898225939, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "her view, it stems from humans' tendency to personify inanimate objects: we", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6060597681884633, "w": 0.8261530750873282, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "create machines based on representations of ourselves, imagine that machines", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6343901559839935, "w": 0.8260987368618117, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "think and behave as we do, and therefore see them as an autonomous threat. 'One", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6627576239083618, "w": 0.8261641477823392, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "of the consequences of thinking that the problem lies with machines is that ….", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6909396534671467, "w": 0.8216287514008753, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "we tend to imagine they are greater and more powerful than they really are", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.7192700035412843, "w": 0.76591812685269, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "and subsequently they become so.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.747600429058207, "w": 0.3617134964771913, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "This led on to the third question, 'Should we be scared by advances in artificial", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7858686308748994, "w": 0.8258810763848841, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "intelligence?' To this question, Rees replied, 'Those who should be worried are the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8141990563918221, "w": 0.8265914717897976, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "futurologists who believe in the so-called \"singularity\".** ... And another worry is", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8425294064659596, "w": 0.8262648272869755, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "that we are increasingly dependent on computer networks, and that these could", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8708845017735845, "w": 0.8260772066215126, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "behave like a single \"brain\" with a mind of its own, and with goals that may be", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8992148518477221, "w": 0.826258778314701, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "contrary to human welfare. I think we should ensure that robots remain as no more", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9275452019218596, "w": 0.8260555738562598, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}